cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "EAVES: Elevation-Area-Volume Estimation from SRTM"
abstract: >
  EAVES reconstructs reservoir elevation-area-volume (EAV) curves for
  ungauged dams in arid regions from SRTM topography acquired in
  February 2000, before most of the dams were built. An automated wall
  placement of up to six stages, starting at the catalog coordinate,
  seeds a flood fill to the spillway elevation or to the level at which
  volume reaches catalog capacity, and a power law V = c·A^b is fitted
  to the area-volume pairs of the fill. Dams without a reliable
  SRTM-derived fit receive regionally calibrated curves anchored to
  design capacity, which pair a regional exponent with a full-pool area
  predicted from catalog and terrain features. The open-source Python
  pipeline transfers to other regions with a DEM that predates most of
  their dams, a river network and a dam catalog. It re-fits the
  regional parameters on the reliable curves of local dams built after
  the DEM acquisition, whereas the placement and acceptance constants
  and the quality thresholds, set on SRTM and the Saudi catalog, need
  re-evaluation for each new region. This release generates the EAVES
  dataset (https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20728128) and accompanies the
  paper that describes it.
